nse in Depth","\u002Fplatform\u002Fdefense-in-depth","02.platform\u002F06.defense-in-depth",{"title":176,"path":177,"stem":178,"icon":179},"MCP Tools","\u002Fplatform\u002Fmcp-tools","02.platform\u002F07.mcp-tools","i-lucide-bot",{"title":181,"path":182,"stem":183,"icon":184},"Observability","\u002Fplatform\u002Fobservability","02.platform\u002F08.observability","i-lucide-activity",{"title":186,"path":187,"stem":188,"icon":189},"Contributing","\u002Fplatform\u002Fcontributing","02.platform\u002F09.contributing","i-lucide-git-pull-request",{"title":191,"path":192,"stem":193,"icon":194},"System Migrations","\u002Fplatform\u002Fsystem-migrations","02.platform\u002F10.system-migrations","i-lucide-database-zap",{"title":196,"path":197,"stem":198,"icon":199},"Service Call Liveness","\u002Fplatform\u002Fservice-call-liveness","02.platform\u002F11.service-call-liveness","i-lucide-heart-pulse",{"title":128,"icon":129,"path":201,"stem":202,"children":203,"page":36},"\u002Fplatform\u002Freference","02.platform\u002F12.reference",[204,209,214],{"title":205,"path":206,"stem":207,"icon":208},"CRI Format","\u002Fplatform\u002Freference\u002Fcri-format","02.platform\u002F12.reference\u002F01.cri-format","i-lucide-link",{"title":210,"path":211,"stem":212,"icon":213},"Grind Jobs","\u002Fplatform\u002Freference\u002Fgrind-jobs","02.platform\u002F12.reference\u002F02.grind-jobs","i-lucide-workflow",{"title":215,"path":216,"stem":217,"icon":151},"Project Publishing Design","\u002Fplatform\u002Freference\u002Fproject-publishing-design","02.platform\u002F12.reference\u002F03.project-publishing-design",{"title":219,"path":220,"stem":221,"icon":222},"Development Server","\u002Fplatform\u002Fdevelopment-server","02.platform\u002F13.development-server","i-lucide-server-cog",{"id":224,"title":33,"body":225,"description":512,"extension":513,"links":514,"meta":515,"navigation":516,"path":34,"seo":517,"stem":35,"__hash__":518},"docs\u002F01.apps\u002F03.application-structure\u002F03.artifact-types.md",{"type":226,"value":227,"toc":502},"minimark",[228,237,241,244,249,273,278,289,292,296,303,307,315,319,334,337,341,344,348,356,360,368,372,375,379,384,388,393,397,400,404,409,413,421,425,428,499],[229,230,231,232,236],"p",{},"Every project in a Kinotic application contributes one or more ",[233,234,235],"strong",{},"artifacts",". An artifact is a typed output that the platform knows how to build, deploy, and manage. This page describes each artifact type and when to use it.",[238,239,59],"h2",{"id":240},"persistence",[229,242,243],{},"The most common starting point. A persistence artifact defines your domain models (entities) and gets auto-generated CRUD services in return.",[229,245,246],{},[233,247,248],{},"What you provide:",[250,251,252],"ul",{},[253,254,255,256,260,261,264,265,268,269,272],"li",{},"Entity classes decorated with ",[257,258,259],"code",{},"@Entity"," and field-level annotations like ",[257,262,263],{},"@NotNull",", ",[257,266,267],{},"@Precision",", and ",[257,270,271],{},"@AutoGeneratedId",".",[229,274,275],{},[233,276,277],{},"What the platform provides:",[250,279,280,283,286],{},[253,281,282],{},"Full CRUD operations (save, find, delete) with pagination and sorting.",[253,284,285],{},"Named queries derived from method naming conventions.",[253,287,288],{},"Automatic storage provisioning and indexing.",[229,290,291],{},"Persistence is typically the first artifact you create because it establishes the data model that the rest of the application builds on.",[238,293,295],{"id":294},"microservice","Microservice",[229,297,298,299,272],{},"A microservice artifact is long-running code that executes in a pod or VM. It publishes services that other parts of the application can discover and call through ",[300,301,302],"a",{"href":52},"service proxies",[229,304,305],{},[233,306,248],{},[250,308,309,312],{},[253,310,311],{},"TypeScript classes that implement your business logic.",[253,313,314],{},"Service interfaces that you want to expose to the rest of the application.",[229,316,317],{},[233,318,277],{},[250,320,321,324,331],{},[253,322,323],{},"Automatic service registration in the Service Directory.",[253,325,326,327,330],{},"Service discovery and zone-based routing so other projects can call your service through a ",[300,328,329],{"href":52},"service proxy"," with a simple function call.",[253,332,333],{},"Lifecycle management, scaling, and health monitoring.",[229,335,336],{},"Use a microservice when your logic goes beyond simple CRUD -- orchestrating across multiple entities, calling external APIs, or running long-lived workflows.",[238,338,340],{"id":339},"batch-job","Batch Job",[229,342,343],{},"A batch job artifact is code that runs on a schedule. It is ideal for periodic tasks like data aggregation, report generation, cleanup routines, or syncing with external systems.",[229,345,346],{},[233,347,248],{},[250,349,350,353],{},[253,351,352],{},"TypeScript code that performs the job.",[253,354,355],{},"A schedule definition (cron expression or interval).",[229,357,358],{},[233,359,277],{},[250,361,362,365],{},[253,363,364],{},"Scheduled execution with retry and failure handling.",[253,366,367],{},"Logging and observability for each run.",[238,369,371],{"id":370},"ui-component","UI Component",[229,373,374],{},"A UI component artifact produces reusable building blocks that can be shared across multiple frontends within the application. Think of it as an internal component library.",[229,376,377],{},[233,378,248],{},[250,380,381],{},[253,382,383],{},"Reusable UI components packaged for consumption by frontend projects.",[229,385,386],{},[233,387,277],{},[250,389,390],{},[253,391,392],{},"Versioning and distribution within the application.",[238,394,396],{"id":395},"frontend","Frontend",[229,398,399],{},"A frontend artifact is a complete user interface that gets deployed as a static site. It consumes services published by other projects in the application.",[229,401,402],{},[233,403,248],{},[250,405,406],{},[253,407,408],{},"A web application (built with any framework) that compiles to static assets.",[229,410,411],{},[233,412,277],{},[250,414,415,418],{},[253,416,417],{},"Static hosting with CDN distribution.",[253,419,420],{},"Automatic connection to the application's services through the Kinotic client libraries.",[238,422,424],{"id":423},"combining-artifact-types","Combining Artifact Types",[229,426,427],{},"Most real-world applications combine several artifact types. A typical setup might look like this:",[429,430,431,447],"table",{},[432,433,434],"thead",{},[435,436,437,441,444],"tr",{},[438,439,440],"th",{},"Project",[438,442,443],{},"Artifact Type",[438,445,446],{},"Role",[448,449,450,463,475,487],"tbody",{},[435,451,452,458,460],{},[453,454,455],"td",{},[257,456,457],{},"data",[453,459,59],{},[453,461,462],{},"Defines entities and provides auto-generated CRUD services",[435,464,465,470,472],{},[453,466,467],{},[257,468,469],{},"services",[453,471,295],{},[453,473,474],{},"Implements business rules that orchestrate across entities",[435,476,477,482,484],{},[453,478,479],{},[257,480,481],{},"jobs",[453,483,340],{},[453,485,486],{},"Runs nightly data aggregation",[435,488,489,494,496],{},[453,490,491],{},[257,492,493],{},"web",[453,495,396],{},[453,497,498],{},"The main user interface",[229,500,501],{},"Each project is independently developed and versioned, but they all deploy as part of the same application and communicate through the Service Directory.",{"title":503,"searchDepth":504,"depth":504,"links":505},"",2,[506,507,508,509,510,511],{"id":240,"depth":504,"text":59},{"id":294,"depth":504,"text":295},{"id":339,"depth":504,"text":340},{"id":370,"depth":504,"text":371},{"id":395,"depth":504,"text":396},{"id":423,"depth":504,"text":424},"Learn about the different artifact types a Kinotic project can contribute -- from persistence and microservices to frontends.","md",null,{},true,{"title":33,"description":512},"ks4mH_HWM4uaDA9Vwx-yIdl366mKkKWDw9PgfC_UDoU",[520,522],{"title":29,"path":30,"stem":31,"description":521,"children":-1},"Learn how to configure Kinotic applications and the projects that compose them.",{"title":25,"path":44,"stem":45,"description":523,"children":-1},"How services work in Kinotic and the communication patterns they support.",1789507130321]